; Quests (read by src/quest.c at boot; "reload quests" rereads it).
;
; Each quest starts with "#<vnum> <title>".  Number quests in the range of
; the zone they belong to (zone 30: 3001-3099), like rooms and mobiles.
; Lines starting with ';' are comments, and the file ends with '$'.
;
;   giver <mob vnum>      who offers it and takes it back (every copy of
;                         that mobile does)
;   level <min> [<max>]   offered from level min; past max (default
;                         min + 15) it pays less, and 10 levels past max
;                         it isn't offered at all
;   daily                 may be done again each day (town errands)
;   after <quest vnum>    only offered once that quest is done
;
; and one objective:
;
;   kill <mob vnum> <n>     slay n of them (the killer's group in the room
;                           gets the credit too)
;   fetch <obj vnum> <n>    bring n of them back (give them to the giver,
;                           or QUEST COMPLETE in his presence)
;   visit <room vnum>       find the room, then report back
;   deliver <mob> <obj>     the giver hands over obj (93 a sealed letter,
;                           94 a wrapped parcel, 95 a small leather pouch,
;                           96 a stoppered flask); giving it to the mob
;                           completes the quest
;   escort <mob> <room>     a new copy of the mob follows the player; the
;                           quest is done when it reaches the room with him
;                           (the mob then says the "done" line and leaves),
;                           and failed if it is killed.  Give escorts their
;                           own mob, not one that is loaded elsewhere, and a
;                           room mobiles may enter; the giver can't hand it
;                           out while standing in that room.
;
; and optionally
;
;   limit <minutes>         real minutes from taking it on; not done in time,
;                           the quest fails (it can be taken on again)
;
; and the words:
;
;   offer <text>    what the giver says when asked about it (several
;                   offer lines run together into one speech)
;   done <text>     what the giver (or recipient) says at the end
;
; Start the text with '*' for narration ("*The fungus folk sway..."), shown
; as it is rather than as speech; text with a '"' in it is narration too.
;
; Rewards: with no "reward" line, gold and experience are worked out from
; the level and the objective (default_reward() in quest.c: generous,
; 5-10 kills' worth of experience at the player's own level, a third of
; that for daily errands; escorts 8; a time limit adds a quarter to the gold
; and one kill's worth).  "reward <gold> <kills' worth of exp> [<obj>]"
; sets them by hand.
;
; Text may not contain '$'.  Quest givers in a zone with no mobiles of its
; own were added to that zone's mobile file and reset.

